#lang r7rs
;; r7rs-gc threads, stage C (docs/archive/r7rs-gc-threads-plan.md): eight
;; threads assoc and dissoc Scheme values in one shared Turmeric persistent
;; map through a mutex, and allocate garbage between turns, while a ninth
;; churns garbage and large objects.  Every slow path of the heap runs under
;; contention: refills, the HAMT's frees on dissoc, large objects, and the
;; collections all nine trigger, each stopping the other eight wherever they
;; are.  The turns are serialized by the mutex, so the map's final contents
;; are the same whichever thread took which turn, and every value is checked
;; whole.
(import (scheme base) (scheme write) (stress) (turmeric crew))
(crew-run)
(write (checksum)) (newline)
